WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.833 --> 00:00:14.500
I wait to get started on my new invention.

2
00:00:15.461 --> 00:00:18.463
I also couldn't wait to fix Oliver's bad attitude.

3
00:00:19.503 --> 00:00:21.784
He was complaining about everything.

4
00:00:21.804 --> 00:00:30.653
"You should have an elevator in your building," he said as we climbed the stairs to my apartment

5
00:00:30.753 --> 00:00:31.854
after the shoe store.

6
00:00:31.874 --> 00:00:36.156
"Or at least an escalator," he added.

7
00:00:36.176 --> 00:00:39.197
"Oliver is driving me crazy!"

8
00:00:39.257 --> 00:00:39.717
I thought.

9
00:00:44.179 --> 00:00:46.701
heard of an escalator in an apartment building?"

10
00:00:51.343 --> 00:00:53.904
are your radiators so loud?"

11
00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:57.682
Oliver asked after we were inside our apartment.

12
00:00:57.702 --> 00:01:01.424
"The heat at my house is really quiet."

13
00:01:02.804 --> 00:01:04.725
Actually Oliver was right about that.

14
00:01:05.866 --> 00:01:09.228
Our radiators were banging and clanking louder than ever.

15
00:01:09.248 --> 00:01:14.651
I figured I'd better start working on my Amazing Attitude Adjuster right away.

16
00:01:16.292 --> 00:01:18.873
But first I had to get Oliver to be quiet.

17
00:01:18.893 --> 00:01:23.315
"Hey, Oliver, do you want to watch TV?"

18
00:01:23.335 --> 00:01:24.316
I asked.

19
00:01:25.292 --> 00:01:26.472
"I can turn it on for you."

20
00:01:30.153 --> 00:01:33.154
TV is really small," said Oliver.

21
00:01:33.174 --> 00:01:35.135
"You need a new one."

22
00:01:36.215 --> 00:01:38.316
"You need a new attitude!"

23
00:01:38.756 --> 00:01:39.256
I thought.

24
00:01:40.536 --> 00:01:45.057
Even though our TV is small, Oliver finally settled down to watch cartoons.

25
00:01:46.338 --> 00:01:49.379
A few minutes later Molly brought me her toy telephone.

26
00:01:50.639 --> 00:01:54.380
I brought it into my room and started working on my dial-a-joke invention.

27
00:01:55.676 --> 00:01:59.017
At my desk I took out a pencil and a thick pad of paper.

28
00:02:00.037 --> 00:02:02.938
I had thought a lot about the way my invention was going to work.

29
00:02:03.898 --> 00:02:05.179
I'll tell you about that later.

30
00:02:06.519 --> 00:02:09.520
The most important thing was that the jokes had to be funny.

31
00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:14.101
They had to make people laugh so they would get a better attitude.

32
00:02:15.161 --> 00:02:20.563
If someone had a really bad attitude, though, she or he might need a lot of jokes.

33
00:02:21.743 --> 00:02:25.044
I decided I would need at least one-hundred jokes for Oliver.

34
00:02:25.996 --> 00:02:27.637
This was not going to be easy!

35
00:02:27.657 --> 00:02:30.877
I went into my brother's room.

36
00:02:32.278 --> 00:02:34.418
He was listening to music with his earphones.

37
00:02:34.438 --> 00:02:39.840
"Tate!" I yelled loudly so he would hear me.

38
00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:42.301
"Do you know any more jokes?"

39
00:02:43.461 --> 00:02:44.941
"What?" yelled Tate.

40
00:02:46.442 --> 00:02:47.342
I yelled louder.

41
00:02:47.362 --> 00:02:50.583
"I said, do you know any more jokes?"

42
00:02:52.483 --> 00:02:54.104
Tate took out his earphones.

43
00:02:54.836 --> 00:02:56.918
"I know a great joke," he said.

44
00:02:56.938 --> 00:03:01.361
"What did the big fish do to his pesky little brother?"

45
00:03:02.241 --> 00:03:03.502
"What?" I asked.

46
00:03:04.583 --> 00:03:05.323
Tate grinned.

47
00:03:05.343 --> 00:03:07.985
"He told him to go jump in a lake!"

48
00:03:09.226 --> 00:03:12.428
That was Tate's way of telling me to stop bothering him.

49
00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:17.431
But I added Tate's joke to my list anyway.

50
00:03:20.654 --> 00:03:22.255
Oliver was still watching TV.

51
00:03:22.995 --> 00:03:23.976
I went into the kitchen.

52
00:03:25.792 --> 00:03:28.234
My mom was sitting at the kitchen table reading a book.

53
00:03:29.535 --> 00:03:33.319
"Mom, can I knock on apartment doors and ask people for jokes?"

54
00:03:33.819 --> 00:03:34.260
I asked.

55
00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:38.223
"Huh?" She looked up from her book in confusion.

56
00:03:38.463 --> 00:03:39.724
I repeated my request.

57
00:03:39.744 --> 00:03:43.688
"Okay," she said slowly.

58
00:03:43.708 --> 00:03:49.393
"But go with Molly, or Josh and Jenny, and stay in our apartment building."

59
00:03:50.494 --> 00:03:52.456
I knew all the neighbors in our building.

60
00:03:53.388 --> 00:03:55.770
But there were only ten apartments, including ours.

61
00:03:58.972 --> 00:04:02.155
We were going to have to work hard to get one-hundred jokes.

62
00:04:03.195 --> 00:04:05.617
Well, ninety-nine, if you counted Tate's.

63
00:04:06.758 --> 00:04:08.700
I heard Oliver's TV show end.

64
00:04:12.402 --> 00:04:15.184
Then Oliver shouted, "I'm bored!

65
00:04:15.545 --> 00:04:17.186
I don't have anything to do!"

66
00:04:18.347 --> 00:04:19.688
I pretended I hadn't heard him.

67
00:04:21.856 --> 00:04:25.059
I opened the door and raced out of the apartment as fast as I could.

68
00:04:26.039 --> 00:04:28.481
I hated to admit it, but Tate was right.

69
00:04:29.482 --> 00:04:32.564
Being a big brother was much harder than being a little one.

70
00:04:33.725 --> 00:04:37.708
Luckily, my Amazing Attitude Adjuster was going to fix that.

71
00:04:38.769 --> 00:04:42.032
It was also going to get me into the Inventor's Hall of Fame!
